WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.860
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.970
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:17.540
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:26.310
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.060
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.530
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.400
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.130
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.800
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.480
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:01.150
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.520
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:12.160
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.070
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:22.310
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:32.420
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.150
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:41.890
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:32.600
1st Investigation Section.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.840
Yes...Yes...

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.070
What?!

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.970
Assistant Inspector! Takashi
Sonobe's regained consciousness!

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:41.780
He has?!

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.650
"The Cursed Children"

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:22.450
<i>Eyes Rutherford-san has just
arrived at Narita Airport!</i>

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.060
Just look at the huge crowd of reporters!

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.330
<i>The pianist Eyes Rutherford-san made
his first trip to Japan yesterday</i>

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.460
to give a recital.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.860
He debuted at 14.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.500
In no time at all, he earned the title
of "brilliant pianist" in America,

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.600
and last year he became
extremely famous in Japan

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.340
after appearing in a car commercial...

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.010
His piano solo album sold an
unprecedented 1 million copies nationwide,

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.810
making him the literal poster
child of the piano world.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:51.150
<i>The 17-year old, one-fourth British
Eyes Rutherford-san's recital</i>

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.020
will take place at 6:00 PM
today at Center Recital Hall.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:59.110
<i>Eyes-san, could we get a word? Eyes-san!</i>

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:00.620
"Newspaper Office"

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.920
"Newspaper Office"
La la la! Time for TV Shopping!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:10.250
Our first item today is this
7-piece Wonder Knife set!

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.230
It's easy to hold, and its
sharpness is unparalleled!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.670
It can even cut this big
dictionary with one slice!

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.470
From cucumber slicers to daikon peelers,

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.900
this 7-piece Wonder Knife set has it all!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:26.210
Buy now and we'll throw in an
anti-bacterial cutting board

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.110
and these high-quality
paulownia drawers for free!

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.910
<i>-Call now! The number is-
-I have breaking news, Narumi-san!</i>

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.820
Quiet. I can't hear the phone number.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.320
You're actually going to call?

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.920
It's a 7-piece Wonder Knife set!

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.590
And it comes with an anti-bacterial
cutting board and paulownia drawers!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.030
The cutting board makes sense,

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:48.100
but what do drawers have to do with knives?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.070
Don't ask me.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.530
Speaking of not letting me do stuff...

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:56.670
<i>Come on, Narumi-san! Let me hear
you play the piano just once!</i>

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:00.680
I know that you used to be
called the "Angel's Fingertips"

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.350
and that you carried the entire
Japanese piano world on your back...

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:09.220
Come on, let me hear you play! Please?!

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.020
You're getting on my nerves!

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.990
So you'll play for me?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.690
I gave up the piano...

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.260
Okay! Our next item is a
3-piece pressure cooker set!

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.260
You gave up playing in front of people,

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:24.500
not piano-playing altogether, right?

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.660
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.200
Take this! My deadly Hiyono Punch!

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.380
I thought you had some breaking news.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:41.120
<i>Oh, yeah! Apparently
Sonobe-sensei is conscious again.</i>

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.450
What? Really?!

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.920
Yes.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.110
I see...

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.060
What do you call a pair
of identical wrinkles?

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:50.630
Twinkles! Get it?!

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:54.430
Whenever you're deep in thought
these wrinkles come out...

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.400
Stop playing with people's wrinkles.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:06:00.990
Somebody bring me the
younger Narumi brother.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:04.070
"Eyes Rutherford Piano Recital"

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.610
"Eyes Rutherford Piano Recital"
Why are you...

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.780
"Eyes Rutherford Piano Recital"
He said "somebody"...

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:12.610
"Eyes Rutherford Piano Recital"
As head of the newspaper,
I planned to interview him anyway,

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.950
"Eyes Rutherford Piano Recital"
so I decided to bring you
too while I was at it!

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.490
Uh huh.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.040
Okay, let's go!

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:28.460
It's him! It's really Eyes Rutherford!

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.780
That was a fancy way of getting me here.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:50.850
What do you want?

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.590
Play.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.320
What?

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.860
Let me hear you play the piano.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:59.730
I wish to hear how well the
Narumi name actually measures up

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.760
to the myths about you in the piano world.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:05.970
Sorry. I gave up the piano a long time ago.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.400
Quit lying.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.070
Yours are the hands that have
been possessed by the piano.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:15.410
They conceal your passion for the
instrument you continue to play.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.910
You play it.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.880
What are you so afraid of?

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:25.090
Is recognizing that you're no comparison
to your brother that frightening?

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:28.120
You've been blessed with a gift...

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:31.430
But you, yourself, know

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.760
that your skills are at best
an imitation of your brother's.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.670
You don't even begin to
compare to the original.

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:40.000
<i>Who is this guy?</i>

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.570
<i>Why is he referring to my brother?</i>

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:45.840
<i>He talks almost like he knows him...</i>

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.780
<i>Does he know about him? What?</i>

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.440
<i>What does he know about my brother?!</i>

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:56.950
Ayumu Narumi.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.320
You will forever be a loser.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:15.200
<i>You're not going to listen
to the recital, Narumi-san?</i>

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.210
I don't have a ticket...

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:21.840
Ta-dah! The lady at the
counter gave me some!

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:24.780
Oh, wait!

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.750
Ayumu Narumi-san, right? Here you are!

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:32.420
That's my name on the envelope!

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.360
Who on earth are they from?!

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.060
Just put the details to the side...

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.560
Stop messing with my details!

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:44.630
I bet they're presents from God!

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:48.400
He must've wanted me to
hear Eyes Rutherford's piano

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:51.110
since you won't play for me!

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.610
Give me a break.

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:54.410
The show will begin in one hour.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.950
The auditorium is now open.
Please take your seats.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:01.350
<i>Let's go, Narumi-san!</i>

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.680
<i>Wow! Front row seats, Narumi-san!</i>

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:11.490
Thank you for giving us
such great seats, God!

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:14.120
I'm super deeply moved!

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.970
<i>An iris!</i>

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.480
<i>What's that, Narumi-san?</i>

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:27.460
Dunno.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.880
Is that what I think it is?

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.990
It's a little too dangerous
to be a present from God.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:39.790
Heya, I'm a Chinese turtle!

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:42.320
The name's Lucky! Don't forget it now!

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.160
As you can see, this is a time bomb.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.230
It contains 200 kilograms of explosives,

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.370
so even the roof will go
bye-bye if it goes off!

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:53.270
Where are the security guards?!
We need to call for the police!

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:56.940
Not so fast! If you call the
police it'll explode on the spot.

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:58.740
It wouldn't matter if
you called them anyway.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.580
Their bomb disposal unit couldn't
handle this kind of bomb.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:06.250
Besides, take a look at the
timer. You're almost out of time.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:09.280
Don't get too flustered, it
won't be that easy to stop.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.650
Tamper with it and it goes boom.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:16.190
There's only one way to stop it -
by pressing the 9 disarmament keys.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:17.960
See those keys there?

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:21.230
All you need to do is press
all nine in a certain order.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.130
What are we going to do?!

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.830
There is only one correct order.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.840
Naturally, it'll go off
instantly if you mess up!

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:33.240
As a special service I'll tell
you the first key to press.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:35.280
Don't worry.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.310
You can disarm it just fine if you
have wisdom, courage, and luck.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:41.450
There are plenty of hints; even
a turtle could figure it out!

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.820
What the hell?!

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:44.750
Is something the matter?

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:48.360
Alright. I'll give you
another big freebie.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:50.760
See the stick coming out of the box?

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:53.730
If you grab that, the time limit
will be extended to 30 minutes.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:56.530
But once you grab it, you can't let go.

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.200
There's a heat sensor attached to it,

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:01.400
so the instant you let go, kaboom!

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.710
What the?!

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.110
<i>Grab it, if you dare!</i>

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:08.580
But once you do, there's no running away!

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.750
Unless you successfully disarm it,
you'll be blown to smithereens!

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.450
Not even your bones would be left!

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:15.280
So what will you do?!

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:17.390
This is insane! Let's get out of here!

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.320
No, there's no time!

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:25.730
Is recognizing that you're no comparison
to your brother that frightening?

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:28.460
Alright, brave hero! Grab it!

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:30.990
You will forever be a loser.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:35.830
I'm...I'm...

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:39.270
I'm!

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.980
You will forever be a loser.

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:54.120
Evacuate everyone in the auditorium!

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.130
And try not to let anyone
know what's going on here!

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.560
And no contacting the police,
no matter what!

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:01.260
Right!

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.590
Hiyono!

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:16.480
We are currently conducting a
cleaning inspection in the auditorium.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.950
We appreciate your patience.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:30.030
Hey.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.160
Yes?

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.660
You're stupid.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:33.600
Come again?

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.460
Why'd you volunteer for
such a dangerous role again?

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:39.940
What's wrong with doing that?
You can disarm it, after all.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.140
You heard Lucky the Turtle, right?

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:44.940
He said you can disarm it if you
have wisdom, courage, and luck.

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:47.440
<i>In which case, you can
do it, Narumi-san!</i>

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:48.740
Don't be stupid.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:52.010
Do you have any idea how many
possible key combinations there are?

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:54.220
40,320!

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:55.820
Forty thousand?!

00:12:55.820 --> 00:13:00.780
Nobody would ever make that kind
of bet if their life was at stake!

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:05.990
<i>The grid of keys...
The number's location...</i>

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.560
<i>Are there any other hints?</i>

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.900
<i>And why a turtle puppet?</i>

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.230
<i>Narumi-san...</i>

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:15.940
<i>You're thinking as hard
as you can, aren't you?</i>

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:19.460
<i>After all, those wrinkles
of yours are showing...</i>

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.450
What was your motive for trying
to kill Sayoko Shiranagatani?!

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:31.120
Why did you have to kill her?

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:35.060
Did someone put you up to it? If so, who?!

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.590
Answer me!

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.330
Takashi Sonobe! Who exactly are you?!

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:40.000
Assistant Inspector!

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:40.890
Answer me!

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.970
<i>Say, Narumi-san.</i>

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:55.610
Why do you tell people you quit the piano?

00:13:55.610 --> 00:14:01.340
It's a waste. You have a
gift, and you play so well...

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:07.620
When I heard it that one
time, I thought to myself,

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:11.230
"What beautiful music.
I wonder who's playing it?"

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:16.960
It was you playing the piano, wasn't it?

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:20.870
You heard that guy.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.440
<i>You mean Eyes-san?</i>

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:25.110
My performances are an
imitation of my brother's.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.510
I can't make my own sound
come out, no matter what I do...

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:33.250
Your skills are an imitation
of your brother's, at best.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:38.190
But it's not like I tried
to imitate him or anything...

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.060
Just whenever I played my own style,

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:43.120
it wound up being just like my brother's...

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:46.260
Pretty soon I realized that everything
I did was the same as my brother.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:49.530
<i>Not just the piano. Everything.</i>

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:53.600
And although I was like him,
he was far superior to me.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:57.770
No matter how hard I try,
I'll never compare to him.

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:01.730
"Is recognizing that you're no comparison
to your brother that frightening?"

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:08.080
Even though I hate the piano,
it reminds me of the reality

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:13.320
that everything I want belongs to him...

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:16.050
That's why playing the
piano is difficult for me.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:22.460
But I can't give it up completely either.

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:26.030
Do you hate your brother?

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.240
I respect him.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.870
He could do anything.
He knew all sorts of things...

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:39.810
<i>Wait! He told me about
something a long time ago!</i>

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:43.680
<i>China, a turtle, nine keys...</i>

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.260
<i>A grid and numbers...</i>

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.750
<i>Could this be that?!</i>

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:57.670
Time to disarm the bomb.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.970
What do you mean by "cursed children"?!

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:02.670
What do you know?! Answer me, Sonobe!

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:05.970
The cursed children must be killed...

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:06.910
Assistant Inspector?!

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.930
The Blade...Children...

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:20.920
<i>Kiyotaka...</i>

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:26.380
<i>Will your brother really be the
key to saving the Blade Children?</i>

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:35.270
The grid of keys, and the
turtle puppet and its name...

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:37.140
Lucky the Turtle?

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:41.630
Yeah, I can actually associate
specific numbers with the grid now.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:46.050
There's a legend in China
that goes like this...

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:51.790
A Xia-dynasty emperor found a turtle
on the bank of the Yellow River.

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:55.190
Its shell was divided into 9 parts,

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:59.060
and for some reason, there
were dots in each part.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:04.200
When the emperor looked
at the number of dots,

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.670
he saw that their sum was always the same

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.100
when added in vertical,
horizontal, or diagonal lines.

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:10.340
That's-

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.540
the story of the mysterious Magic Squares.

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:17.350
A Magic Square is a square grid in
which the sum of a line of numbers -

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.350
whether it be vertical,
horizontal, or diagonal -

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.120
always comes out the same.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:25.550
In the case of a 3x3 grid,
the sum is always 15.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:31.290
In a 3x3 grid with 9 slots, there
are only 8 possible arrangements.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:35.360
And there are only two where 1 comes here...

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:39.100
If I punch in one of those two
combinations I should be able to disarm it.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:41.100
<i>You're amazing, Narumi-san!</i>

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:44.770
But there's no way to
tell which one it is.

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.710
Just like the turtle said...

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.180
It all comes down to luck...

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:52.950
Oh, so that's why his name is Lucky!

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:55.550
But I don't believe in luck.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.790
There's a 50% chance of death.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:18:00.050
Don't resent me if I mess up.

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:04.190
Don't worry! You're not the kind of
person to die in a situation like this!

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:06.420
<i>I believe in you, Narumi-san!</i>

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.760
Here goes.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:18.140
<i>When people put numbers in order,</i>

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:22.010
<i>they generally prefer to start from
low numbers and then count upward.</i>

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:26.010
<i>But the person who made
this is pretty crafty.</i>

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.280
<i>In which case...</i>

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:34.710
The disarm keys go like this.

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:54.040
Hey.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:54.980
Yes?

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.510
I don't want any more
of this sort of thing.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:18:59.950
We did succeed, but still...

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:06.090
Congratulations on disarming
the bomb, Little Narumi!

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:09.350
The Blade Children have
been waiting for you.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:15.430
Narumi's younger brother
disarmed Rio's bomb?

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:16.430
Yeah...

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:18.600
Hey, isn't that going a little overboard?

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:20.740
There's no need to rush,
if we just give him time...

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.760
We have no time. Bye.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:30.880
Not the curse's mark again...

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:36.250
We now present Eyes
Rutherford's piano recital.

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:06.450
"The cursed children must be killed....

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:08.250
The Blade Children..."

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:13.320
"Little Narumi! The Blade
Children have bee waiting for you!"

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.720
<i>What are the Blade Children?</i>

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.260
<i>What are the Blade Children?</i>

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.600
-You're hiding something, aren't you?!
-You're hiding something, aren't you?!

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:23.800
Admit it!

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:25.330
No, you!

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:26.630
Just tell me!

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:28.800
No, you first!

00:21:07.030 --> 00:21:12.740
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:19.440
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:37.600
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:43.240
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:49.140
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:55.710
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:55.710 --> 00:22:01.450
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:06.660
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:12.500
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:24.110
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:29.880
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:36.190
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:40.620 --> 00:22:44.520
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:45.960
Out of the frying pan and into the fire!

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:47.490
Curses, like chickens, come home to roost!

00:22:47.490 --> 00:22:49.230
Fortune comes to those who smile!

00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:51.030
In that same spirit, the
highlight of the next episode

00:22:51.030 --> 00:22:54.230
<i>is Hiyono-chan's rapid-fire gag attack</i>

00:22:54.230 --> 00:22:57.540
<i>meant to make the always-sullen
Narumi-san smile!</i>

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.100
Boom! Boom! Boom!

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:01.370
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:01.370 --> 00:23:02.910
The Happiness of Those Who Believe

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:04.510
You'll regret it if you miss it!

00:23:04.510 --> 00:23:07.170
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
